  {
   "id": "founding",
   "text": "Legend says Rome was founded in seven fifty-three BC by Romulus, who was raised with his twin brother Remus by a she-wolf. The real story is humbler: farming villages on hills beside the river Tiber. To the north lived the rich Etruscans, in cities like Tarquinia and Volterra. To the south, Greek settlers had built Naples and Syracuse.",
