  {
   "id": "society",
   "text": "So who were the Romans? At the top stood the patricians, old noble families who filled the Senate. Most citizens were plebeians: farmers, craftsmen and traders, who struggled for generations to win equal rights. Merchants grew rich on trade. And at the bottom were enslaved people, often captured in war, with almost no rights at all.",
