  {
   "id": "punic",
   "text": "But across the sea stood Carthage, a rich trading city in North Africa with a mighty navy. In two sixty-four BC, Rome and Carthage went to war over Sicily. They would fight three wars, on and off, for more than a century. The prize was the whole western Mediterranean.",
   "scene": {
    "type": "era",
    "year": "264 BC",
    "title": "Rome vs Carthage",
    "sub": "The Punic Wars",
    "icons": [
     "fluent-3d:ship",
