  {
   "id": "hannibal",
   "text": "In two eighteen BC, the Carthaginian general Hannibal set out from Cartagena, in Spain, with a large army and dozens of war elephants. He crossed the Pyrenees and then the snowy Alps, and invaded Italy. At Cannae, in two sixteen BC, he crushed one of the largest armies Rome had ever raised. But Rome refused to surrender. Its general Scipio struck back in Africa and defeated Hannibal at Zama, near Carthage, in two oh-two BC.",
