  {
   "id": "growth",
   "text": "Now watch Rome grow. In two sixty-four BC, it ruled only Italy. By two oh-one BC, it also held Sicily, Sardinia and much of Spain. In one forty-six BC, it destroyed both Carthage and the Greek city of Corinth. And by forty-four BC, Roman lands circled the Mediterranean, from Spain to Syria. The Romans called it simply Mare Nostrum, our sea.",
