  {
   "id": "crisis",
   "text": "But the Republic was built to run a city, not an empire. Generals grew richer than the state, and their soldiers were loyal to them, not to the Senate. For about a hundred years, Rome was torn by riots, rivalries and civil wars. Then one general changed everything.",
   "scene": {
    "type": "era",
    "year": "49 BC",
    "title": "The Republic Cracks",
    "sub": "Generals, riots and civil war",
    "icons": [
