     "lib:soldiers-168"
    ],
    "cue": "Republic"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "caesar",
   "text": "Julius Caesar. He spent eight years conquering Gaul, today's France and Belgium, and won a famous siege at Alesia in fifty-two BC. In forty-nine BC, he led his army across the Rubicon river into Italy, breaking the law and starting a civil war. He defeated his rival Pompey at Pharsalus, in Greece, and in Egypt he backed Cleopatra as queen, in Alexandria.",
