  {
   "id": "ides",
   "text": "In forty-four BC, Caesar was named dictator for life. Weeks later, on the Ides of March, a group of senators assassinated him. Another civil war followed. Caesar's adopted heir, Octavian, ruled the West from Rome. His rival, Mark Antony, ruled the East, side by side with Cleopatra, queen of Egypt. Only one side could win.",
   "scene": {
    "type": "split",
