     "cue": "Antony"
    },
    "vs": "VS"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "augustus",
   "text": "The showdown came at Actium, off the coast of Greece, in thirty-one BC. Octavian's fleet won. A year later, his army took Alexandria, and Egypt became Roman. Back in Rome, in twenty-seven BC, the Senate gave Octavian a new name: Augustus. He never called himself king, but he was Rome's first emperor.",
