  {
   "id": "pompeii",
   "text": "Not everything was peaceful. In seventy-nine AD, Mount Vesuvius erupted near Naples. Ash and hot gas buried the towns of Pompeii and Herculaneum. Tragic for the people who lived there, but a gift to history: today we can still walk their streets, and see their bakeries, shops, graffiti and painted walls.",
