   "id": "peak",
   "text": "Under the emperor Trajan, in one hundred seventeen AD, the empire reached its greatest size. It stretched from Britain to the Persian Gulf, and from the Rhine and the Danube to the Sahara. Trajan conquered Dacia, in today's Romania, and marched all the way into Mesopotamia. Tens of millions of people, speaking dozens of languages, lived under Roman law.",
