   "text": "To save it, Emperor Diocletian shared power among four rulers, based in cities like Trier, Milan and Nicomedia. Then Constantine took control. In three thirteen AD, an agreement made in Milan granted Christians freedom of worship, and Constantine himself became a Christian. In three thirty, he gave the empire a new capital in the east: Constantinople, today's Istanbul.",
