   "text": "Germanic peoples crossed the Rhine and the Danube. In four ten, the Visigoths sacked Rome, the first time in about eight hundred years that a foreign enemy had taken the city. The Vandals seized Carthage and sacked Rome again in four fifty-five. Finally, in four seventy-six AD, the general Odoacer removed the last Western emperor, a boy called Romulus Augustulus, at Ravenna. The Western Roman Empire was over.",
