   "text": "Emperor Justinian won back Italy, where his mosaics still shine in Ravenna, and North Africa, including Carthage. In Constantinople, he built the Hagia Sophia, finished in five thirty-seven, the largest church in the world for nearly a thousand years. Slowly, the empire shrank. And in fourteen fifty-three, the Ottoman sultan Mehmed the Second captured Constantinople. After more than two thousand years, the last Roman state was gone.",
